DOS-PORT (patch 0105, Phase 10 SAFETY revert). Reverts slot 0104's
default-flip from auto_select back to organya for env-unset / empty
SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_BACKEND. KEEPS the auto-detect chain code in
place -- explicit AUDIO_BACKEND=auto still engages it for opt-in.

Background -- real-HW W22-WB-C iter findings 2026-05-06:

The Stage-5 auto-detect chain (slot 0104) probes WB FIRST. Real-HW
iter on g2k Vibra16S CT2490 + DreamBlaster S2 daughterboard found
sdl-engine's SDL_DOSMpu401Init hangs INDEFINITELY on real S2 hardware
(probe sends MPU-401 reset 0xFF -> expects ACK 0xFE -> S2 either does
not ACK or ACKs at unexpected timing -> busy-loop never terminates).
Default DOSKUTSU.EXE under default-flip = default lockup at "Loading"
splash on g2k = unacceptable safety regression.

sdl-engine triaging the WB probe issue in parallel (SDL/0042+ fix in
flight); expect 1-2 iter cycles to land + validate. Until that fix
ships AND validates clean on real-HW iter, default DOSKUTSU.EXE must
be safe to run without operator action -- i.e., must default to
organya (Phase 10 baseline, pre-Stage-5 behavior).

What this patch does:
- selectBackendFromEnv: env-unset / empty -> organya (was auto_select
  at slot 0104). Single-line behavioral change.
- Added LOG_INFO narration: "audio backend: organya (default; Phase
  10 baseline). Auto-detect chain available via SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_-
  AUDIO_BACKEND=auto for opt-in; default reverted to organya in patch
  0105 pending real-HW WB probe fix (sdl-engine SDL/0042+)."
- Updated AUDIO_BACKEND=auto branch's log narration with explicit
  warning: "NOTE: WB probe is known-broken on real DreamBlaster S2
  hardware as of 2026-05-06; operators with S2 may want to use
  AUDIO_BACKEND=opl3 instead until that fix lands."

What this patch DOES NOT do (kept in place per team-lead dispatch):
- The auto-detect chain code in SoundManager::init (slot 0104) is
  unchanged. AUDIO_BACKEND=auto still runs WB -> OPL3 -> Organya
  probes in sequence. Operators who want Phase 10 audio offload AND
  have validated their hardware doesn't hit the WB-probe-hang can
  opt in via the explicit env value.
- The `auto_select` enum value (slot 0104) stays in place; just no
  longer selected by default.
- Per-backend instantiation logic, helper statics, OPL3/WB backend
  classes, MidiScheduler, MidiBackendStub -- all intact.

Restore-default plan:
When sdl-engine ships the WB probe fix in SDL/0042+ AND it validates
clean on real-HW iter (probe terminates with deterministic
success/failure within <=10 ms), a follow-up patch (slot 0107+) will
flip the default back to auto_select by changing the env-unset/empty
branch in selectBackendFromEnv to return auto_select again. This is
a one-line revert pending the validation gate; the chain
infrastructure is fully ready.

Smoke (DOSBox-X-fast, 6 gates):

  Gate 1 -- AUDIO_BACKEND unset (NEW DEFAULT = organya): logs
    "audio backend: organya (default; Phase 10 baseline)..."; no
    chain attempted; engine runs organya path. 39 flips, no crashes.
    **The safety-critical gate -- confirms default DOSKUTSU.EXE is
    safe to run on g2k without operator-set env var.**
  Gate 2 -- AUDIO_BACKEND=auto (explicit, opt-in): chain still works;
    "auto-detect: probing wb..." -> "wb backend ready" -> "auto-detect:
    wb selected." Slot 0104 functionality preserved for opt-in users.
    38 flips, no crashes. Note narration explicitly warns about WB
    probe issue on real S2.
  Gate 3 -- AUDIO_BACKEND=organya forced: regression unchanged. 38
    flips, no crashes.
  Gate 4 -- AUDIO_BACKEND=wb forced: regression unchanged; direct
    install. 39 flips, no crashes.
  Gate 5 -- AUDIO_BACKEND=opl3 forced: regression unchanged; probe
    fails under DOSBox-X -> graceful organya fallback. 38 flips, no
    crashes.
  Gate 6 -- AUDIO_BACKEND=midi-stub forced: regression unchanged.
    39 flips, no crashes.

All 6 gates PASS.

Phase 10.5 backlog (deferred per team-lead dispatch):
  - OPL3 silent music triage (operator W22-WB-C PLAY3 confirmed
    OPL3 backend ran clean but no audible music). Hold for
    flush-instr verdict on "OPL3 actually integrated vs silently
    fell back" before substantial debugging. Patch slot 0106+
    reserved for this fix once root cause identified.
  - Restore default-to-auto when SDL/0042+ WB probe fix ships +
    validates real-HW. One-line revert in selectBackendFromEnv.
  - Idle-pause coordination, fuller GM bank, velocity/CC dispatch
    refinements -- all still pending Phase 10.5 prioritization.

Per CLAUDE.md `silent_narrow_pattern.md`: this revert IS a default-
behavior narrowing of slot 0104's scope, but it is NOT silent -- the
explicit team-lead dispatch 2026-05-06 mandated this revert as an
URGENT/SAFETY task in response to the W22-WB-C iter regression.
Memorialized in commit message + LOG_INFO narration so the temporary
nature is obvious to any future reader of the code or DEBUG.LOG.
